# Tailwind important modifiers

This project uses **Tailwind CSS v4**. Prefer the canonical important form that IntelliSense suggests.

## Rule

- **Do:** put `!` at the **end** of the utility: `min-h-11!`, `px-3!`, `text-sm!`
- **Don't:** put `!` at the **start**: `!min-h-11`, `!px-3`, `!text-sm`

Arbitrary values follow the same pattern: `min-h-[3.25rem]!` (or the scale equivalent such as `min-h-13!` when IntelliSense offers it).

Variants keep the important on the utility token:

- Correct: `hover:bg-surface!`, `md:min-h-11!`
- Wrong: `hover:!bg-surface`, `md:!min-h-11`

## Examples

```html
<!-- Wrong -->
<button class="btn btn-primary !min-h-9 !px-3 !py-1.5">Ask</button>

<!-- Right -->
<button class="btn btn-primary min-h-9! px-3! py-1.5!">Ask</button>
```

```ts
// Wrong
[ngClass]="cond ? '!border-accent-cyan/50 !text-accent-cyan' : ''"

// Right
[ngClass]="cond ? 'border-accent-cyan/50! text-accent-cyan!' : ''"
```

Do **not** change CSS `!important` declarations in stylesheets, TypeScript/Angular `!` (non-null / negation), or attribute bindings like `[disabled]="!canSend()"`.
